{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_a63zqigcqplqwfudlfgrifeztrahircdxqsv4wsm23tay23hn4eq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Rust translation builds cleanly in both debug and release mode. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nI translated the C `dict` library (a runtime-generic hash map supporting multiple key types) to safe, idiomatic Rust by replacing every `unimplemented!()` body in `src/dict.rs`.\n\n### Key design choices\n\n- **Storage**: Replaced C linked-list buckets (`dict_list_t` with `dict_elem_t*` chain) with `Vec<DictElem>` per bucket — equivalent semantics, no `unsafe`, automatic memory management.\n- **Keys/values**: Stored as `Vec<u8>` to retain the C library's \"type-erased bytes\" generic behavior.\n- **Hashing**: Reproduces C's `dict_get_hash` byte-for-byte for primitive types (with proper sign-extension for `char`/`wchar`/`i32`/`i64`) and the polynomial rolling hash (`code = code*256 + b mod 1e9+7`) for `Str`/`Struct`.\n- **Reshape**: Mirrors C semantics — triggered when bucket size *after* push exceeds `mod`, with new size `mod * step * DEFAULT_STEP`. Uses `mem::replace` to safely transfer old buckets to new layout.\n- **Serialization**: Matches C wire format exactly: 3 `u32`s (key_size, val_size, count) followed by entries. For `Str`, the entries are `(u32 len, val_bytes)` pairs followed by a separate string-data section.\n- **Deserialization**: Validates key/val sizes, rebuilds entries, then reshapes if any bucket grew too large (matching C's post-load reshape logic).\n- **`dict_destroy`**: Calls user-provided destructors for keys (only when `copy` was set, matching C) and values.\n- **`dict_key`**: Returns a leaked `&'static [u8]` snapshot of all keys, mirroring the C contract that the caller frees the buffer.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `cargo build` — clean compile\n- `cargo build --release` — clean compile\n- No `unsafe`, no FFI, no `unimplemented!()`/`todo!()`/`panic!()` placeholders left (the only `panic!` calls are for the same data-corruption error paths the C code reported on `stderr`)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":254,"cache_read_input_tokens":54777,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":254,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e58d72a9-dd42-4c95-a810-bef4501f4859","uuid":"802f9c5e-a077-4aba-be5e-252a60e7c24f"}
